<header><p class="enc-kicker">Place · region</p><h1 class="enc-title">Cyprus</h1></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Cyprus is a large island in the eastern <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/mediterranean">Mediterranean</a>, valued for its <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/copper">copper</a>. In the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/late-bronze-age">Late Bronze Age</a> it corresponded with <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/egypt">Egypt</a> in the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/akhetaten">Amarna</a> diplomatic letters of the Egyptian Empire <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/new-kingdom-of-egypt">New Kingdom</a>. Under <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/muawiya-i">Muawiya</a>, the first Arab navy of the early <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/umayyad-caliphate">Umayyad Caliphate</a> raided Byzantine Cyprus.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/cyprus.jpg" alt="Cyprus" width="320" height="214" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: İsmet Güney, SVG by User:Vzb83~commonswiki · Public domain · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Flag_of_Cyprus.svg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
